# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# Solana Mobile Saga (ingot): keep the three audio SoundWire buses awake.
#
# The two WSA883x speaker amplifiers (bus 3250000) enumerate at boot, but
# the first time the bus's clock is stopped and started again (its runtime
# suspend, a few seconds after the last use) both drop to device number 0
# at once, the controller's enumeration fails ("SWR bus clsh detected",
# interrupt bit 11) and they stay unattached: every later stream plays into
# nothing. The WCD938x's buses (3210000 playback, 33b0000 capture) survive
# the same restart, but with parity errors and alerts, and an alert on the
# playback side ends in a NULL dereference in the codec's interrupt
# callback (the kernel's SoundWire IRQ thread dies).
#
# With runtime power management held on, the clocks never stop. This costs
# idle power and does not cover a system suspend, where the clocks stop
# anyway. Remove this file once the kernel keeps the devices across a
# clock stop.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="platform", KERNEL=="3210000.soundwire|3250000.soundwire|33b0000.soundwire", ATTR{power/control}="on"
